{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd","id":1486311,"title":"Updating \"Immortal: The Gathering\" for CofD.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-12T15:53:50-07:00","id":1486311,"title":"Updating \"Immortal: The Gathering\" for CofD.","content":"So sometime ago someone on the boards was trying to updated this fan splat for &quot;Highlander&quot;-style immortales in what was then the NWOD: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20140313192250/http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Misc/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20140313...es_Revised.pdf</a><br /> <br /> And here is the thread for those who are curious: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/26156-world-of-darkness-immortal-the-watcher-chronicles-immortal-in-the-gmc\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...tal-in-the-gmc</a><br /> <br /> That thread seems to have been abandoned which is a shame as I always like the OWOD fan-splats for Immortals and the one for NWOD has one of my favorite machanics for immoral healing. <br /> <br /> For those unaware, there are a few differences between Immortals in the Movies and the TV series, which some of the older fan-works tried to blend in. For example: <br /> Film<br /> 1. Do not experience \u2018First Death\u2019. Connor Macleod never actually died even when initially stabbed by the Kurgan \u201cand last night you were all but a corpse\u201d were the words uttered by one of his clansmen. At some point in their lives the immortality gene \u2018kicks in\u2019, and with it certain properties.<br /> <br /> 2. Do not suffer temporary death o any kind. No matter what kind of damage Connor suffered he automatically got up straight afterwards \u2013 getting shot by Nazi he awoke immediately telling the young Rebecca to be quiet; and stabbing himself in the heart to show Brenda his immortality.<br /> <br /> 3. Heal instantly from any wound, including severed limbs. It is never stated in the film they do not, plus over several thousand years of sword fights you\u2019ll lose a limb or two.<br /> <br /> 4. Are capable of absorbing huge amounts energy, this is shown in the film where Connor is sent to hilltop to absorb lightning strikes. The roof sign had fallen and electrified the water while both immortals continued to fight and were seen to absorb the electricity.<br /> <br /> 5. Slightly stronger than normal humans. For instance when Connor was in the police station, he was surrounded, one officer grabbed his arm. Martial ability aside, Connor just raised his arm to shake the officer off which resulted in the police officer letting go and tumbling across the room.<br /> <br /> 6. Have a connection to every living thing, man or animal.<br /> <br /> <br /> Highlander Immortals TV Series<br /> <br /> 1. First Death. In order for immortality to trigger they must experience a violent death and this can be at any age although usually events conspire to make the new immortal young.<br /> <br /> 2. Immortals can sense Pre-Immortals, Duncan ad Richie.<br /> <br /> 3. Heal from any wound except severed limbs. Xavier St Cloud was forced to attach a hook. <br /> <br /> 4. Should they suffer massive trauma, or fatal damage for a normal human they will suffer temporary death; during this time their body goes into dormancy healing the damage.<br /> <br /> 5. Cannot absorb energy like the film version and are susceptible to temporary death by electrocution.<br /> <br /> The NWOD FanSplat for immortals had something that acted as both a balance and a way to move between these extremes. See the healing rules on p. 40 for details.<br /> Basicaly an immortal here heals 1B of damage every minute and 1L every hour and 1A every day (well it doesn't say that, but it is a reasonable assumption on my part). When in the presence of another immortal (like say for a duel) or when using a point of Edge (their name for the supernatural fuel here), the immortal heals 1B every turn, 1L every minute, and 1A every hour. If that isn't enough, the immortal can spend 1 Edge to remove any single wound no matter the level. <br /> <br /> Again I find this to be a nice compromise between how healing was portrayed in the original film and the TV series.<br /> <br /> Other things I liked:<br /> <br /> On p. 21 we get a description of the Power Stat, Kenning, and I must say, the fluff on it is well done. <br /> <br /> However, this was made for the original NWOD, and now since we are in CofD, I think some things need an upgrade. For example, alot of the Immortal's &quot;tricks&quot; in the original seem to only work on other immortals. These were based on how Immortals in the franchise could sense each other, but only each other, and influence them. For this upgrade, we could have more like the original film and have these tricks work on other living creatures (though that means Vamps and Emphermals are immune). <br /> <br /> Any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T17:47:45-07:00","id":1486314,"title":"","content":"What about using the Purified from CoD 1e: Immortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T18:07:16-07:00","id":1486318,"title":"","content":"I would say it would be a good idea to look at <i>World of Darkness: Immortals</i> for a reference on how to codify mechanically and to cross reference when fine tuning balance.<br /> <br /> In this case specifically, one major thing is missing is the price. Immortality must always have a price. The Blood Bathers, for example, need to completely bathe in blood from time to time, with more complex and inflexible conditions for the ritual granting more supernatural advantages. Body Thieves can only stay in the same body for so long before starting to lose their grip on it, some rely on mystical baubles to jump hosts, they activate all their abilities with Willpower. The Purified are able to reassemble themselves after death and get spirit powers, but can be eaten by the denizens of the Shadow like anyone else (I think they might be the closest thing to what you want). There are more but I think you get the idea.<br /> <br /> The Highlanders don't seem to suffer a downside to their abilities. Their regeneration is second only to werewolves, what resource fuels it ? What bane can shut it down ? They return from death, what can kill them for good ? I would recommend decapitation, translated into taking more lethal or aggravated damage on a called head shot than their Stamina rating. Now snipers will make them nervous.<br /> <br /> There is no need for the Buzz, unless you want them to hunt each other. Then a reward could be 2 XP that can only be used to buy dots in skill the defeated Highlander had. Buzz radius could be Wits x 10 meters.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I would recommend making the resource that fuels their active powers be something that they have to go out of their way to replenish, something that could get them in trouble or make them cross paths with other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T06:44:44-07:00","id":1486338,"title":"","content":"Just to make a quick post, I notice the link in the original post is from a web archive. That fan book is still on my site. Here's a link if anyone needs it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T15:37:29-07:00","id":1486469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1486338#post1486338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make a quick post, I notice the link in the original post is from a web archive. That fan book is still on my site. Here's a link if anyone needs it:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Immortal_Rules_Revised.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/p...es_Revised.pdf</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> I agree with you that having their head destroyed should count as decapitation. Also yeah the original suppliment didn't seem to have any mechanics for replenishing Edge that I could see, though I might need to double check. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> I could see a downside that their blood can be used to boost any blood ritual, and that hunters like the Instatite Alchemists or the Ascending Ones also get a boost to their Alchemical works if they use it as an ingrediant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T16:48:22-07:00","id":1486475,"title":"","content":"Worth noting for the current conversation is that in Highlander, the cost of immortality <i>is</i> that immortality-the burden of time is a fucker.<br /> <br /> The simplest way to express that in Chronicles, and I say this without reading the update and not having read the original in years, is to leave the Immortals with Integrity. No special buffer to the horrors and losses they experience over time, just Immortal, now get fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T18:43:32-07:00","id":1486481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1486475#post1486475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting for the current conversation is that in Highlander, the cost of immortality <i>is</i> that immortality-the burden of time is a fucker.<br /> <br /> The simplest way to express that in Chronicles, and I say this without reading the update and not having read the original in years, is to leave the Immortals with Integrity. No special buffer to the horrors and losses they experience over time, just Immortal, now get fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. Off course we could take a cue from the Immortals V5 suppliment and have a Detachment meter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T18:55:35-07:00","id":1486483,"title":"","content":"I second Arcane's idea, that captures the weariness of the ages perfectly. No special dispensation except for your own powers, while being painfully aware that you still need to survive. Quiescence, Sybaris and Lunacy mess with your memory, but you have no way to become immune to it, but know you need to survive things you can't even evaluate with your own eyes.<br /> <br /> In the topic of Edge, I would instead simply use Willpower to fuel their abilities. There isn't really anything supernatural that is thematically connected to Highlander. So indulging their Vice helps them armor up emotionally to face the dangers of immortality, playing out their Virtue restores their inner reserves of strength. Plus, one point recharges per night's sleep, so they recover slowly. It builds upon the foundation Arcane created by reinforcing that they are still very much connected to mortals than most supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T19:52:53-07:00","id":1486487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1486483#post1486483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I second Arcane's idea, that captures the weariness of the ages perfectly. No special dispensation except for your own powers, while being painfully aware that you still need to survive. Quiescence, Sybaris and Lunacy mess with your memory, but you have no way to become immune to it, but know you need to survive things you can't even evaluate with your own eyes.<br /> <br /> In the topic of Edge, I would instead simply use Willpower to fuel their abilities. There isn't really anything supernatural that is thematically connected to Highlander. So indulging their Vice helps them armor up emotionally to face the dangers of immortality, playing out their Virtue restores their inner reserves of strength. Plus, one point recharges per night's sleep, so they recover slowly. It builds upon the foundation Arcane created by reinforcing that they are still very much connected to mortals than most supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was just thinking that. I remember in the original that there was a special rule called &quot;Enlightened Will&quot;. Basically the Immortals &quot;Kenning&quot; could be used as part of the dice pool once it was higher than the usual benifits Willpower gave. This can tie into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T06:39:28-07:00","id":1486514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1486469#post1486469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're very welcome!<br /> <br /> And should you need me to make an updated sheet once you get things worked, let me know and I'll see what I can do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T13:48:53-07:00","id":1486795,"title":"","content":"So any more ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T01:08:18-07:00","id":1488442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1486795#post1486795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So any more ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought it would be cool to have different kinds of immortals as an x-splat. So:<br /> <br /> \u25cfRegenerators: Regular highlander type immortals. Happens when a pre immortal dies by murder or smth, can be permakilled only in they way they first died.<br /> <br /> \u25cfReincarnators: Can't really think of much besides being body surfers.<br /> <br /> \u25cfPhylacteries: Immortals whose immortality is tied to an object held dear in their first life. Can only be killed by destroying said object.<br /> <br /> \u25cfSanctuaries: Immortals who have a specific place in which they 'respawn' after getting killed or dying in an accident or whatever.Can only be killed when in their sanctuary. The Good news is that said sanctuary can be moved around(albeit with great difficulty).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T11:33:22-07:00","id":1488474,"title":"","content":"We already have the other Immortals suppliment. Right now I would like to focus on Highlander-style immortals. <br /> <br /> Your comment on x-splats does make me wonder if y-splats are necessary for this though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T17:29:04-07:00","id":1488511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1488474#post1488474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have the other Immortals suppliment. Right now I would like to focus on Highlander-style immortals.<br /> <br /> Your comment on x-splats does make me wonder if y-splats are necessary for this though?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're supposed to be rare, right? Then probably not 'group' type splats where you have a membership. Something like Refinements / Hungers / Agendas would make more sense.<br /> <br /> I'd personally have the alternate types as not Highlander (x-)splats, but just a different type of Immortal altogether. Then bring all of them, including Highlanders themselves, under the Immortal umbrella as Mummy 2e details. Their superpowers could be represented by the Arisen's Affinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T21:53:49-07:00","id":1488532,"title":"","content":"I do think your concept of Refinments/Agendas ect, was in the original document. <br /> A part of me really wants to keep the unique feel of the Highlander Immortals, like the Classic WoD supplement did. That said I would like to have a Steryotpe section about how one kind of Immoratal reacts to the other types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:05:56-07:00","id":1488948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1488474#post1488474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have the other Immortals suppliment. Right now I would like to focus on Highlander-style immortals. <br /> <br /> Your comment on x-splats does make me wonder if y-splats are necessary for this though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the NWoD version of immortal has 'codes' as the Y-splat. Basically how immortals deal with the existence of the game. Less organisations, more personal beliefs, hence the term code","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T09:50:29-07:00","id":1489347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1488948#post1488948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the NWoD version of immortal has 'codes' as the Y-splat. Basically how immortals deal with the existence of the game. Less organisations, more personal beliefs, hence the term code</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Make it more clear that they aren't cliques then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T02:52:15-07:00","id":1489539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1489347#post1489347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Make it more clear that they aren't cliques then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ye, especially since 'The Game' is still a thing so large scale immortal organisations are simply suicidal. <br /> <br /> Also what do you think abt getting rid of the buzz? I feel like that could make 'The game' more high stakes, especially if you consider my x-splat ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T21:19:55-07:00","id":1490484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1489539#post1489539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ye, especially since 'The Game' is still a thing so large scale immortal organisations are simply suicidal.<br /> <br /> Also what do you think abt getting rid of the buzz? I feel like that could make 'The game' more high stakes, especially if you consider my x-splat ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it is such a part of the mythos that getting rid of it feels wrong. Though we could make it that feeling other immortals is automatic though honing in on them requires a roll at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T11:49:21-07:00","id":1490636,"title":"","content":"I vote against getting rid of the Buzz. Immortals have no special characteristics to differentiate them from everyday mortals, apart from any body type changes from natural human mutation and those happening due to lifestyle changes from the era the immortal was born in. It would prolong the Game needlessly, add red herrings and make it easy for those not interested to go underground, especially because they will perfect their skills with ages of practice. Its why it was a deliberate choice in Highlander and its an iconic passive power.<br /> <br /> Regarding a Y axis, here are rough drafts for some of their possible schools of thought:<br /> <br /> 1- Immortals that embrace the likelihood of death in the Game, so they build legacies that will outlast them. Have a higher focus on crafts and science. From creating cures, to stunning works of art, to novel cooking styles, new engineering techniques or even generation defining movies. (The Jettators from the cartoon series would be found here)<br /> <br /> 2- Those that focus entirely on the Game, focusing on learning the fighting techniques, gathering bleeding edge gear, preparing contingencies and proactively going on the hunt. Have an easier time accessing Armory, Safe Place and fighting style instruction. (The Kurgan would probably be one)<br /> <br /> 3- The ones that decide to live their lives to the maximum, searching for success and new experiences, surrounding themselves in false identities that are too well known for others to move against. Have an easier access to Alternate Identities, Fame and Resources. (Ramirez would be found on the low key end of their spectrum)<br /> <br /> 4- Occultists that believe the supernatural holds all answers. Why are they immortal ? What is the nature of the Prize ? How to survive the Game ? What other rules does this contest enforce ? They have a tendency to obtain Libraries (and their Advanced variation), Esoteric Armories, Contacts in their field of study and Retainers with occult specialties (often those studying immortality rituals)<br /> <br /> 5- Those that abstain from the game entirely, or only make a move after careful deliberation. Have a tendency to be Anonymous, Untouchable, Investigative Prodigies and Trained Observers (Methos is an example)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-18-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T04:18:44-07:00","id":1490864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1490636#post1490636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vote against getting rid of the Buzz. Immortals have no special characteristics to differentiate them from everyday mortals, apart from any body type changes from natural human mutation and those happening due to lifestyle changes from the era the immortal was born in. It would prolong the Game needlessly, add red herrings and make it easy for those not interested to go underground, especially because they will perfect their skills with ages of practice. Its why it was a deliberate choice in Highlander and its an iconic passive power.<br /> <br /> Regarding a Y axis, here are rough drafts for some of their possible schools of thought:<br /> <br /> 1- Immortals that embrace the likelihood of death in the Game, so they build legacies that will outlast them. Have a higher focus on crafts and science. From creating cures, to stunning works of art, to novel cooking styles, new engineering techniques or even generation defining movies. (The Jettators from the cartoon series would be found here)<br /> <br /> 2- Those that focus entirely on the Game, focusing on learning the fighting techniques, gathering bleeding edge gear, preparing contingencies and proactively going on the hunt. Have an easier time accessing Armory, Safe Place and fighting style instruction. (The Kurgan would probably be one)<br /> <br /> 3- The ones that decide to live their lives to the maximum, searching for success and new experiences, surrounding themselves in false identities that are too well known for others to move against. Have an easier access to Alternate Identities, Fame and Resources. (Ramirez would be found on the low key end of their spectrum)<br /> <br /> 4- Occultists that believe the supernatural holds all answers. Why are they immortal ? What is the nature of the Prize ? How to survive the Game ? What other rules does this contest enforce ? They have a tendency to obtain Libraries (and their Advanced variation), Esoteric Armories, Contacts in their field of study and Retainers with occult specialties (often those studying immortality rituals)<br /> <br /> 5- Those that abstain from the game entirely, or only make a move after careful deliberation. Have a tendency to be Anonymous, Untouchable, Investigative Prodigies and Trained Observers (Methos is an example)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering whether the nameless* need some sort off designated villains or not. Like pure for werewolves or pandorans for promethean and whatnot.<br /> <br /> *My idea for nicknaming the immortals. It supposed to show how due to living forever immortals have to always change identities. Hence never having a proper name from birth to death (which they can't experience unless violently by another one of their kind). Hence the term 'nameless'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","user":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","date":". 08-21-2022, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T07:33:33-07:00","id":1490879,"title":"","content":"<b>Looks at how much of vampire society exists due to ennui</b><br /> I think they will cause a lot of messes by the nature of the Game, collision of ideas and opposing ambition. The Game means every other member is a potential rival or threat, it may lead towards everyone acting with high vigilance.<br /> <br /> &quot;So these guys call themselves Nameless, ever heard of them ?&quot;<br /> <i>Mummy:</i> &quot;You mean have I met them in our Nameless Empire ? I never have, never hasn't, never have had hasn't....what ? You try applying the proper tense to a non-linear perception of time&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:21:19-07:00","id":1490895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1490879#post1490879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Looks at how much of vampire society exists due to ennui</b><br /> I think they will cause a lot of messes by the nature of the Game, collision of ideas and opposing ambition. The Game means every other member is a potential rival or threat, it may lead towards everyone acting with high vigilance.<br /> <br /> &quot;So these guys call themselves Nameless, ever heard of them ?&quot;<br /> <i>Mummy:</i> &quot;You mean have I met them in our Nameless Empire ? I never have, never hasn't, never have had hasn't....what ? You try applying the proper tense to a non-linear perception of time&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit, now I'm wondering if any immortals lived in the time of Irem, and if any of them are still walking the streets tonight...<br /> EDIT: those two mummies talking abt immortals remind me of all those arcadia debates I read a while ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","user":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","date":". 08-22-2022, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:28:18-07:00","id":1490897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1486311-updating-immortal-the-gathering-for-cofd?p=1490895#post1490895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shit, now I'm wondering if any immortals lived in the time of Irem, and if any of them are still walking the streets tonight...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you lived in a place whose word for human meant &quot;sacrifice&quot; and built its philosophy on the Law of Suffering, I imagine any Immortals would want out before being used as self renewing sacrifices, high durability forced labor or citizens trapped in the most dystopian society in unrecorded history. I think that, at the very least, they would have extensive trauma an