small note, you are missing the close parenthesis on the hyperlinks. Anyway, reactions probably vary based on the Highlander, here are some samples:<br /> <br /> &quot;Suffering was your Law, your Judges condemned you to an eternity of service, your patrons eldritch abominations gnawing at eternity. You and I have been puppets in a game we don't understand, its time we got some answers and our freedom&quot; - reaction to the Arisen<br /> <br /> &quot;Elizabeth Bathory was actually working under valid supernatural principles by serially killing, and you follow the trail she blazed ? You live in Dante's circle of violence by your own volition, hell really is other people&quot; - reaction to Blood Bathers<br /> <br /> &quot;You walked death's edge and emerged with your ears open to the world's heartbeats, hungering for actualization. Beware the salivating predators, because unlike us, your suffering doesn't end with losing your head&quot; - reaction to the Purified<br /> <br /> &quot;Your identity is the ship of Theseus, rebuilt countless times as history marches on, shifting a little bit each time. How will you know when its no longer the original ship ?&quot; - reaction to the Body Thieves, Patchwork People and Harvesters<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometimes duty requires someone to guard the gate, sometimes what you really need is an invisible monster that keeps the other monsters at bay&quot; - reaction to the Wardens<br /> <br /> &quot;Dorian Gray thought eternity would be a banquet of hedonism, but madness took him when he could not run from what he had become&quot; - reaction to the Eternals<br /> <br /> &quot;When their story is over, will they take your heartbeat back with them ?&quot; - reaction to the Visitors<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometimes they are humans that looks like beasts, other times they are beasts that look like humans, and eventually they cannot see the line between them&quot; - reaction to vampires","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experience